claim.claim-text:
1. A system comprising:
at least one tank,
a coolant inlet,
a coolant outlet,
a dielectric liquid coolant,
a heat exchanger,
a pump, and
a plurality of computers;
wherein the at least one tank includes at least a portion of the dielectric liquid coolant;
wherein at least portions of the plurality of computers are completely submerged within the dielectric liquid coolant;
wherein the pump is configured to pump the dielectric liquid coolant from the coolant inlet to each of the plurality of computers;
wherein at least a portion of the dielectric liquid coolant flows through the plurality of computers for absorbing at least a portion of any heat being generated by each of the plurality of computers;
where at least a portion of the dielectric liquid coolant exiting the plurality of computers flows through the coolant outlet;
wherein the coolant outlet is configured to enable heated dielectric liquid coolant to flow to the heat exchanger for heat rejection;
wherein the heat exchanger is configured to enable cooled dielectric liquid coolant to flow to the coolant inlet; and
wherein the at least one tank is configured to enable a removal of a computer of the plurality of computers without a need to remove any other computer of the plurality of computers from the at least one tank.

17. The system of claim 1,
further including collection piping;
wherein the collection piping collects heated dielectric coolant flowing out of the plurality of computers.

19. A system comprising:
at least one tank,
a coolant inlet,
a coolant outlet,
a dielectric liquid coolant,
a heat exchanger,
a pump, and
a plurality of computers;
wherein the at least one tank includes the dielectric liquid coolant;
wherein the plurality of computers are completely submerged within the dielectric liquid coolant;
wherein the pump is configured to pump the dielectric liquid coolant from the coolant inlet to each of the plurality of computers;
wherein at least a portion of the dielectric liquid coolant flows through the plurality of computers for absorbing at least a portion of any heat being generated by each of the plurality of computers;
wherein a fluid flow of the dielectric liquid coolant entering the at least one tank through the coolant inlet is initially directed through a volume of liquid coolant at a bottom side of the at least one tank, through the plurality of computers, and into a volume of the dielectric liquid coolant at a top of the at least one tank;
wherein at least a portion of a fluid flow of the dielectric liquid coolant within the at least one tank flows from the top of the at least one tank to a bottom of the at least one tank;
where at least a portion of the dielectric liquid coolant exiting the plurality of computers flows through the coolant outlet;
wherein the coolant outlet is configured to enable heated dielectric liquid coolant to flow to the heat exchanger for heat rejection;
wherein the coolant outlet is located at a top portion of the at least one tank;
wherein the heat exchanger is configured to enable cooled dielectric liquid coolant to flow to the coolant inlet;
wherein the at least one tank is configured to enable a removal of a computer of the plurality of computers without a need to remove any other computer of the plurality of computers from the at least one tank;
wherein the plurality of computers are connected to a computing network; and
wherein the plurality of computers are running software configured to receive a request to provide computing resources.
